### Gate 3 Deep-Dive — `--dry-run` Mutation Issue (Blocking)

Reading `activate_satellite()` (identical pattern in `activate_aggregator` and `activate_wroom`):

```bash
activate_satellite() {
  local dry_run="false"
  [[ "\x24{1:-}" == "--dry-run" ]] && dry_run="true"
  ...
  if [[ "current" == "c3-default" ]]; then
    # Already in mode — goes straight to print_workflow → SAFE ✅
    print_workflow satellite "$dry_run"
  else
    clean_active_configs     # ❌ MUTATES FS — runs regardless of --dry-run
    cp "$BAK_GATEWAY_AGG" …  # ❌ MUTATES FS — runs regardless of --dry-run
    run_render               # ❌ MUTATES FS — runs regardless of --dry-run
    ...
    print_workflow satellite "$dry_run"   # dry_run only guards the pipeline from here
  fi
}
```

**When the board is already in the target mode**, `--dry-run` is fully non-mutating ✅. **When a board switch is required**, `clean_active_configs`, `cp`, and `run_render` all execute before `print_workflow` is reached. Only the 8-step pipeline inside `run_full_pipeline()` is skipped. This was raised as "blocking" by the GPT review and is confirmed by direct code reading at L488–511 (aggregator) and L531–568 (satellite).

